#: ../../operations.rst:71 31cb3a751807413fac7aa56cecb38ab9
msgid ""
"``.github/workflows/ci.yml``'s ``image`` job builds and pushes ``ghcr.io"
"/rewake-fr/api`` and the OCR sidecar ``ghcr.io/rewake-fr/api-ocr`` (from "
"``ocr/``) on every push to ``main`` (never on a PR, and never from any "
"other branch), tagged both ``latest`` and ``sha-<short hash>`` -- the "
"latter never moves, so it's always safe to pin or roll back to. Since the"
" source repo is private, so is the image; the server needs a one-time "
"``docker login ghcr.io`` (a personal access token with ``read:packages``,"
" or a fine-grained token scoped to this repo, as the password) before its"
" first pull -- never done by the deploy script itself, and no credential "
"is ever read or stored by it. ``deploy.sh`` runs ``docker compose pull``,"
" then ``docker compose up -d --remove-orphans``, and waits for "
"``http://localhost:3002/health/`` (15 tries, 2 s apart), printing the "
"``api`` logs if it never answers. ``docker-compose.yml``'s services "
"declare both ``image:`` (what a real deploy pulls) and ``build:`` (what "
"local dev still uses via ``--build``), so either workflow works from the "
"same file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../operations.rst:89 ec09f9afb67946a4a4da6b2c37963459
msgid "Release notes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../operations.rst:91 a548148f7d2042229aa0d806e4ac0c58
msgid ""
"Once the image is pushed, the ``release`` job publishes a GitHub Release "
"tagged with the same ``sha-<short hash>`` (so each release is exactly one"
" deployable image, and its page shows the ``deploy.sh`` command for it). "
"Its notes are rendered by ``scripts/release/release_notes.py`` from the "
"commits since the previous ``sha-*`` release, grouped by Conventional "
"Commits type (``feat``, ``fix``, ``docs``, ``chore``...; anything "
"unprefixed goes under \"Autres changements\"). A commit that requires "
"action at deploy time -- a removed or renamed environment variable, a new"
" Shopify scope -- should say so in a ``BREAKING CHANGE:`` footer (or a "
"``type!:`` subject): it's then listed first, under \"Changements "
"cassants\". Releases run one at a time, in push order; re-running a "
"workflow never overwrites an existing release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../operations.rst:103 7c05c68f485747f8a40b749d2928cfea
msgid ""
"``docker-compose.yml`` runs five services: ``api`` (port 3002), "
"``worker`` (``celery -A api.celery_app worker``) and ``beat`` (``celery "
"-A api.celery_app beat`` -- required once any registered script has a "
"real ``schedule``, currently ``shopify_catalog_reconciliation`` and "
"``airtable_catalog_stats``; its schedule state lives in "
"``/home/rewake/logs/celerybeat-schedule``), all three from the API image "
"and bind-mounting ``/home/rewake/DB`` and ``/home/rewake/logs``; "
"``redis`` (``redis:7-alpine``, ``redis-data`` volume); and ``ocr`` (the "
"label OCR sidecar, internal only on port 8000). The container command "
"uses ``uv run --no-sync``, so nothing tries to reach the network at "
"startup -- the image is built once with ``uv sync --frozen --no-dev`` and"
" run exactly as built."
msgstr ""

#: ../../operations.rst:117 5fac6eb7440a4bc4b17e3c50af39f81b
msgid "Logging"
msgstr ""

#: ../../operations.rst:119 f5fc6eaa94394c65865d899efdb443ad
msgid ""
"``structlog`` renders JSON (or ``console`` for local readability) to "
"stdout and to a rotating file (``LOG_FILE`` in ``api/constants.py``, "
"currently ``/home/rewake/logs/api.log``); falls back to stdout-only if "
"the log directory isn't writable. A request-id middleware "
"(``api/utils/logger.py``) binds ``request_id``/``method``/``path``/ "
"``client_ip`` to every log line for a request and adds ``X-Request-ID`` "
"to the response."
msgstr ""

#: ../../operations.rst:128 41ea798675004533b84c97e851cdd6ad
msgid "CI/CD"
msgstr ""

#: ../../operations.rst:130 d51ca33683004c10b7d39ba0e5f3aaac
msgid ""
"``.github/workflows/ci.yml``'s ``quality`` job runs on every pull request"
" and every push to ``main``: ``uv run ruff check .``, ``uv run mypy api "
"scripts``, and a Sphinx build with ``-W`` (any warning fails it). **Tests"
" are deliberately not run in CI** -- many hit the real Airtable API (no "
"mock layer yet, see :doc:`development`) and need six token/credential "
"secrets to even pass, which turned out to be more fragile than valuable "
"as a required CI gate; run ``make test`` (or ``uv run pytest``) locally "
"with a real ``.env`` instead. See :doc:`development` for other known gaps"
" CI surfaces. Its ``image`` job (build+push to GHCR) only runs after "
"``quality`` passes, and only on a push to ``main``; ``release`` follows "
"``image`` -- see \"Deployment\" above."
msgstr ""

